595
00:39:25.151 --> 00:39:26.431
Production Concerns.

596
00:39:27.681 --> 00:39:28.833
Failure modes.

597
00:39:29.113 --> 00:39:30.457
Here is a quick table:

598
00:39:30.737 --> 00:39:33.020
Failure, and Symptom, and Mitigation.

599
00:39:33.300 --> 00:39:34.580
Compaction starved.

600
00:39:34.860 --> 00:39:35.671
Symptom:

601
00:39:35.951 --> 00:39:37.999
Disk fills, reads slow (L1).

602
00:39:38.279 --> 00:39:39.281
Mitigation:

603
00:39:39.561 --> 00:39:42.249
Headroom, throttled but never paused compaction.

604
00:39:42.529 --> 00:39:45.388
No Bloom filters or too many SSTables.

605
00:39:45.668 --> 00:39:46.479
Symptom:

606
00:39:46.759 --> 00:39:48.231
Slow misses (L1).

607
00:39:48.511 --> 00:39:49.513
Mitigation:

608
00:39:49.793 --> 00:39:51.649
Blooms, compaction strategy.

609
00:39:51.929 --> 00:39:53.167
Tombstone pile-ups.

610
00:39:53.447 --> 00:39:54.257
Symptom:

611
00:39:54.537 --> 00:39:57.460
Slow scans, resurrection after missed repair.

612
00:39:57.740 --> 00:40:02.860
Mitigation: gcgrace versus repair schedule; avoid delete-heavy patterns.

613
00:40:03.140 --> 00:40:04.484
Ack before fsync.

614
00:40:04.764 --> 00:40:05.575
Symptom:

615
00:40:05.855 --> 00:40:07.967
Lost acknowledged writes (L2).

616
00:40:08.247 --> 00:40:09.249
Mitigation:

617
00:40:09.529 --> 00:40:12.175
Group commit; documented durability levels.

618
00:40:12.455 --> 00:40:13.884
Divergent replicas.

619
00:40:14.164 --> 00:40:14.975
Symptom:

620
00:40:15.255 --> 00:40:16.343
Stale reads.

621
00:40:16.623 --> 00:40:17.625
Mitigation:

622
00:40:17.905 --> 00:40:20.487
Hints, read repair, Merkle repair (L3).

623
00:40:20.767 --> 00:40:22.367
Full-range repair at peak.

624
00:40:22.647 --> 00:40:23.457
Symptom:

625
00:40:23.737 --> 00:40:25.124
Network saturation.

626
00:40:25.404 --> 00:40:26.407
Mitigation:

627
00:40:26.687 --> 00:40:28.649
Incremental, throttled, off-peak.

628
00:40:29.999 --> 00:40:32.346
R + W at most N for carts.

629
00:40:32.626 --> 00:40:33.437
Symptom:

630
00:40:33.717 --> 00:40:35.957
Read-your-write violations (L4).

631
00:40:36.237 --> 00:40:37.239
Mitigation:

632
00:40:37.519 --> 00:40:38.735
QUORUM for carts.

633
00:40:39.015 --> 00:40:40.338
W = ALL.

634
00:40:40.618 --> 00:40:41.429
Symptom:

635
00:40:41.709 --> 00:40:44.034
Write outages on any stall (L4).

636
00:40:44.314 --> 00:40:45.317
Mitigation:

637
00:40:45.597 --> 00:40:46.791
QUORUM + hints.

638
00:40:47.071 --> 00:40:49.055
Clock skew with LWW.

639
00:40:49.335 --> 00:40:50.146
Symptom:

640
00:40:50.426 --> 00:40:51.535
Lost updates.

641
00:40:51.815 --> 00:40:52.818
Mitigation:

642
00:40:53.098 --> 00:40:56.106
Vector clocks or CRDTs or single writer.

643
00:40:57.456 --> 00:40:58.544
Observability.

644
00:40:58.824 --> 00:41:05.693
Per node: pending compactions, SSTables per read (histogram), Bloom false-positive rate, disk usage.

645
00:41:05.973 --> 00:41:09.643
Commit-log sync latency, group sizes, dropped mutations.

646
00:41:09.923 --> 00:41:14.232
Hints stored or replayed, read-repair rate, repair progress and bytes.

647
00:41:14.512 --> 00:41:19.568
Per table: latency by consistency level, speculative retries, timeouts.

648
00:41:20.918 --> 00:41:21.857
Security.

649
00:41:22.137 --> 00:41:26.147
Encryption in transit between nodes and clients; at rest on disks.

650
00:41:26.427 --> 00:41:30.822
Authentication and per-keyspace authorisation; no anonymous access.

651
00:41:31.102 --> 00:41:38.718
Backups via snapshots (SSTables are immutable, so hard-link snapshots are cheap), stored off-cluster and encrypted.

652
00:41:40.068 --> 00:41:40.964
Performance.

653
00:41:41.244 --> 00:41:44.359
Token-aware clients (send directly to a replica).

654
00:41:44.639 --> 00:41:49.417
Prepared statements or batching per partition; avoid multi-partition batches.

655
00:41:49.697 --> 00:41:56.353
Size partitions sensibly (for example, 100 MB each); split wide rows by time buckets.

656
00:41:57.703 --> 00:41:58.429
Cost.

657
00:41:58.709 --> 00:42:06.133
Replication factor times space amplification times compaction headroom = real disk per GB of data.

658
00:42:06.413 --> 00:42:09.997
Managed services trade operations for per-request pricing.

659
00:42:10.277 --> 00:42:12.111
Model both at peak and average.

660
00:42:12.391 --> 00:42:15.549
Tiered storage for cold SSTables where supported.

